./tests/misc.rs:1105:// The following two tests show a discrepancy in search results between
./tests/misc.rs:1106:// searching with memory mapped files and stream searching. Stream searching
./tests/misc.rs:1107:// uses a heuristic (that GNU grep also uses) where NUL bytes are replaced with
./tests/misc.rs:1108:// the EOL terminator, which tends to avoid allocating large amounts of memory
./tests/misc.rs:1109:// for really long "lines." The memory map searcher has no need to worry about
./tests/misc.rs:1110:// such things, and more than that, it would be pretty hard for it to match the
./tests/misc.rs:1111:// semantics of streaming search in this case.
