./crates/cli/src/process.rs:139:///
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:140:/// The purpose of this reader is to provide an easy way to execute processes
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:141:/// whose stdout is read in a streaming way while also making the processes'
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:142:/// stderr available when the process fails with an exit code. This makes it
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:143:/// possible to execute processes while surfacing the underlying failure mode
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:144:/// in the case of an error.
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:145:///
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:146:/// Moreover, by default, this reader will asynchronously read the processes'
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:147:/// stderr. This prevents subtle deadlocking bugs for noisy processes that
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:148:/// write a lot to stderr. Currently, the entire contents of stderr is read
./crates/cli/src/process.rs:149:/// on to the heap.
